sg. fem.)","terrific (sg. fem.)"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"אדריכל","en":"architect (m)","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"מפורסם","en":"famous (sg. masc.)","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"שזה","en":"that this is","alt":["that it is"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"דבר","en":"thing","alt":["a thing","speak (imp.)"],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"חיובי","en":"positive (sg. masc.)","alt":[],"from":"lexicon"},{"he":"נחמד","en":"nice","alt":["nice (sg. masc.)","nicely","pleasant (sg. masc.)"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"חזקה","en":"strong","alt":[],"from":"skill"},{"he":"שגויה","en":"wrong (sg. fem.)","alt":["incorrect (sg. fem.)"],"from":"skill"},{"he":"הוא","en":"he","alt":["(he) is","(it) is"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"כלב","en":"dog","alt":["a dog"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"הזה","en":"this","alt":["that"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"הזאת","en":"this","alt":["that"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"אני","en":"I","alt":["I think so","I am","me"],"from":"phrase"},{"he":"חושב","en":"think","alt":["I think so","is thinking","thinks"],"from":"phrase"}],"lexemes":["רגיל","אפשרי","צבאי","זולה","אחראית","זול","הרזֶה","רגילה","רזָה","רציני","העצמאית","שגויות","נחמד","חזק","שגוי","עצמאיים","הנכונה","בלתי אפשרית","מהילדה","עשיר","עצמאי","נחמדה","חזקה","נחמדים","הנכון","בלתי אפשרי","עשירה","החזק","רצינית","שגויה","ועשירה"],"tips":"זקן vs ישן\n------------\nAs you will notice in this lesson, the adjectives זקן (zakén) and ישן (yashán) have the same translation - old.\nBe careful not to confuse the two, because both are extremely common and it will sound quite strange if you confuse them.\n\nישן is used to describe **old inanimate objects** (e.g. old book, old TV, old lamp etc.) and זקן is used to describe **old animate objects** (e.g. old people, old man, old dog etc.)."}